  [38;5;153m${window.SETTINGS.apiBaseUrl}/login[39m. Note [38;5;153mlogin()[39m is currently a stub that only logs — so this change is structural,
  and nothing observable changes at runtime today.

  [1mError handling[0m

  Two cases worth handling, both cheap:

  - [1mUnknown hostname[0m → falls through to [38;5;153mprod[39m. This preserves today's behavior for any deployed host and means a
    forgotten hostname entry degrades to "works, points at prod" rather than "broken."
  - [1m[38;5;153msettings.js[39m missing or not loaded[0m (someone reorders or drops the script tag) → [38;5;153mapp.js[39m should throw a named error at
    call time rather than silently POSTing to [38;5;153mundefined/login[39m. A one-line guard in [38;5;153mlogin()[39m.

  [38;5;153mObject.freeze[39m on the exported object so a later script can't mutate config out from under the app.

  [1mTesting — and a tooling question[0m

  This repo has no test infrastructure: no [38;5;153mdevDependencies[39m, no [38;5;153mscripts[39m, no test directory, nothing to follow. So there's
  a real choice here, and since it's cheapest to decide now, it belongs in the design rather than after it.

  [38;5;153mresolveEnvironment(hostname)[39m is deliberately a pure function taking the hostname as an argument rather than reading
  [38;5;153mwindow.location[39m inline — that's what makes the mapping testable at all, and it costs nothing either way.
